WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.810
6 March 1957.

2
00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:08.090
A British law declares that London will
have no responsibility for governing Ghana.

3
00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:13.090
Ten years earlier, India and Pakistan
became two independent Dominions.

4
00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:18.030
In 1965, Kwame Nkrumah described
a different kind of control.

5
00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.690
He wrote of a state that
is, in theory, independent.

6
00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:27.120
In reality, he wrote, its economy and
politics are directed from outside.

7
00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:30.590
So which kind of power
keeps the world stable:

8
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:34.630
ruling colonies directly, or
pulling strings from afar?

9
00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:37.170
In this mission, you'll
follow power from empire,

10
00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:39.770
through the Cold War, to today.

11
00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:43.650
Then you'll map two rival
blocs, and weigh a world of one,

12
00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:46.110
two or many great powers.

13
00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:50.910
Your mission: decide which pattern
of power keeps the world most stable.
